    "id": "Lidar_DEM_DTM_Veg_Pohnpei_2496_1",
    "stac_version": "1.1.0",
    "description": "This dataset includes a 10-m resolution digital terrain model (DTM) of much of the island of Pohnpei, the largest and highest of the islands in the Federated States of Micronesia (FSM). The vegetation-free DTM was generated by rasterizing the ground-classified points of a point cloud collected during an airborne lidar survey. The instrument was a RIEGL LMS-Q680i, and the aircraft was a Britten-Norman Islander. Additional data include a digital surface model (DSM) comprising elevation measurements associated with the first returns, that is, the highest points in the point cloud data set, which in most parts of the surveyed area will pertain to the forest canopy; a pulse density map, in which each cell of the raster contains a value equal to the number of laser pulses fired by the lidar instrument that were recorded to have fallen within the corresponding 10 m2; and a ground point density map, in which each cell holds the number of points classified as ground. The survey flights took place in July 2023 and February and March 2024. The data are provided in GeoTIFF format.",
